      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Ancient Period"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Andhra history spans early prehistoric settlements, the dominant Satavahana Dynasty, and subsequent rule by Ikshvaku and Pallava empires.",
        "The Medieval period was shaped by powerful dynasties including Eastern Chalukyas of Vengi, Kakatiyas, Vijayanagara Empire, and Qutb Shahis of Golconda.",
        "Modern period transitions include Nizam rule, British influence, and the eventual creation of Andhra State post-Independence.",
        "In 2014, the state underwent major administrative restructuring resulting in the bifurcation and formation of Telangana."
      ],
      "id": "i786acq"
    },
